# What may enter a container image build (docs/mlops.md §8.1).
#
# This is an allow-list: everything is excluded first, then the tracked source folders
# and files are let in one by one. A new top-level folder is therefore NOT in the image
# until it is added here on purpose. Never let in: data/, artifacts/ (data and models are
# mounted or read from Cloud Storage, never copied), .git (the commit comes from a build
# argument), .venv (the image builds its own environment), caches, credentials.
*

!src/
!scripts/
!tests/
!configs/
!results/
!docs/
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!Makefile
!README.md
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md

# Inside the folders let in above: files that git ignores too (.gitignore).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.parquet
**/*.npy
**/*.npz
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.pkl
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/kaggle.json
**/submission*.csv
**/submission*.csv.gz

# Named explicitly although `*` already covers them, so that nobody lets them in by mistake.
data/
artifacts/
.git/
.venv/
